<title>UK: Klaus says high Czech rates depressing growth.</title>
<headline>Klaus says high Czech rates depressing growth.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Czech Prime Minister Vaclav Klaus said his country's high interest rates were depressing the economy and growth this year would be very low. &quot;It is depressing the economy already now and I understand the central bank is trying to make a soft landing,&quot; he told Reuters after a lecture at the London School of Economics.</p>
</text>
